      "area": "age_gating",
      "claim": "A parent reports that Discord requires users to be at least 13 years old, but there is no real age verification beyond entering a birth date, so younger kids can easily sign up if they lie about their age.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "users must be at least 13 years old— in line with U.S. privacy laws (COPPA). But there's no real age verification beyond entering a birth date, so younger kids can easily sign up if they lie about their age."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D521]",
      "area": "age_gating",
      "claim": "A parent reports that Discord turns on some safety features by default for teens age 13 to 17, including blocking direct messages from people they don't know, hiding age-restricted servers and NSFW content, blurring sensitive images, and showing alerts when receiving messages from new contacts.",
      "stance": "mitigation",
      "quote": "For teens age 13 to 17, Discord turns on some safety features by default, including: Blocking direct messages from people they don't know; Hiding age-restricted servers and NSFW (not safe for work) content; Blurring sensitive images, and showing alerts when receiving messages from new contacts."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D521]",
      "area": "contact",
      "claim": "A parent reports that strangers can message a child on Discord, and direct messages from strangers are blocked by default for users aged 13-17, but can be turned on by the user.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "Blocking direct messages from people they don't know"
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D521]",
      "area": "contact",
      "claim": "A parent reports that voice chat is available on Discord and can be used by strangers, but the platform does not have a separate kids mode and 13-year-olds use the same version as adults.",
      "stance": "neutral",
      "quote": "there's no separate \"kids mode,\" and 13-year-olds are basically using the same version of the app as adults—just with a few safety settings that can be changed."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D521]",
      "area": "money",
      "claim": "A parent reports that Discord does not sell games but integrates with platforms like Steam and Xbox, and teens may feel pressure to buy games or in-game items to join in.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "When teens see what their friends are playing, they may feel pressure to buy games or in-game items to join in."
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D521]",
      "area": "data",
      "claim": "A parent reports that Discord collects user data and may share it for ads or with third parties, and the data can be deleted.",
      "stance": "neutral",
      "quote": "Discord doesn't sell games anymore, but it integrates with platforms like Steam and Xbox."
    },
    {
